  (text "⚠ MAGNET-TOPOLOGY DESIGN GATE (mechanical — not an electrical issue):\nThe MT6701 is an ON-AXIS sensor. Per datasheet §6 it reads a Ø6 mm x 2.5 mm diametric CYLINDER\nmagnet centred on the die: air gap 0.5-2.0 mm, field 200-1000 G, off-axis misalignment <= 0.3 mm.\nThe airframe currently mounts it OFF-AXIS at R = 11 mm over a Ø22 ring (wings_s1223_revo.scad) —\nthat is ~37x the 0.3 mm misalignment limit and is OUT OF SPEC for the MT6701.\nRESOLVE before fab: (a) relocate the magnet to a real on-axis shaft END (Ø6 cyl, MT6701 kept), or\n(b) select a genuinely off-axis / side-shaft-rated IC (verify its datasheet first).\nSee ENC-NACELLE-1.md, airframe/wings-nacelles/WBS.md §1.1.3.6, docs/TILT_SPAR_ANALYSIS.md §1/§3.5."
    (at 30.00 128.00 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.25 1.25) (bold yes)) (justify left))
    (uuid "e2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000063"))

